    "reason": "[ev-a7c9af863980] says only that Kafka 4.0.0 is now supported and that support for Kafka 3.8.0 and 3.8.1 is removed. Nothing in the evidence says what happens to clusters still on those versions: it doesn't say the operator stops working, rejects the Kafka resource or blocks the upgrade. So the proposed workload-failure (\"the operator will not function\") claims more than the evidence supports. None of the section-context upgrade notes settle it either: [ev-526028ea7180] and [ev-f432b7205700] cover Kafka 4.0 logging and JMXReporter, not 3.8.x clusters. To decide, we'd need upstream text (such as the upgrade guide or operator behaviour docs) stating how Strimzi 0.46.0 handles a Kafka resource whose version is 3.8.0 or 3.8.1.",
